  <emu-host-law clause="sec-async-function-constructor" class="advice">Advice to programs that subclass the constructor.</emu-host-law>
  <emu-host-law clause="sec-iterable-interface" class="advice">The interface a program's objects conform to: advice to programs, not a requirement on the host.</emu-host-law>
  <emu-host-law clause="sec-iterator-interface" class="advice">The interface a program's objects conform to: advice to programs, not a requirement on the host.</emu-host-law>
  <emu-host-law clause="sec-asynciterable-interface" class="advice">The interface a program's objects conform to: advice to programs, not a requirement on the host.</emu-host-law>
  <emu-host-law clause="sec-asynciterator-interface" class="advice">The interface a program's objects conform to: advice to programs, not a requirement on the host.</emu-host-law>
  <emu-host-law clause="sec-object.prototype.tolocalestring" class="scope">ECMA-402 and what an implementation without it may do: outside the base layer.</emu-host-law>
  <emu-host-law clause="sec-number.prototype.tolocalestring" class="scope">ECMA-402: outside the base layer; without it, the locale-sensitive result is the host choice LocaleNumberString.</emu-host-law>
  <emu-host-law clause="sec-number.prototype.tolocalestring" para="2" class="theorem">Without ECMA-402 the steps read neither optional parameter: a property of the overlay's steps.</emu-host-law>
  <emu-host-law clause="sec-bigint.prototype.tolocalestring" class="scope">ECMA-402: outside the base layer; without it, the locale-sensitive result is the host choice LocaleNumberString.</emu-host-law>
  <emu-host-law clause="sec-bigint.prototype.tolocalestring" para="2" class="theorem">Without ECMA-402 the steps read neither optional parameter: a property of the overlay's steps.</emu-host-law>
  <emu-host-law clause="sec-date.prototype.tolocaledatestring" class="scope">ECMA-402: outside the base layer; without it, the locale-sensitive result is the host choice LocaleDateString.</emu-host-law>
  <emu-host-law clause="sec-date.prototype.tolocaledatestring" para="2" class="theorem">Without ECMA-402 the steps read neither optional parameter: a property of the overlay's steps.</emu-host-law>
  <emu-host-law clause="sec-date.prototype.tolocalestring" class="scope">ECMA-402: outside the base layer; without it, the locale-sensitive result is the host choice LocaleDateString.</emu-host-law>
  <emu-host-law clause="sec-date.prototype.tolocalestring" para="2" class="theorem">Without ECMA-402 the steps read neither optional parameter: a property of the overlay's steps.</emu-host-law>
  <emu-host-law clause="sec-date.prototype.tolocaletimestring" class="scope">ECMA-402: outside the base layer; without it, the locale-sensitive result is the host choice LocaleDateString.</emu-host-law>
  <emu-host-law clause="sec-date.prototype.tolocaletimestring" para="2" class="theorem">Without ECMA-402 the steps read neither optional parameter: a property of the overlay's steps.</emu-host-law>
  <emu-host-law clause="sec-string.prototype.localecompare" class="scope">ECMA-402: outside the base layer; without it, the locale-sensitive result is the host choice LocaleCompare.</emu-host-law>
  <emu-host-law clause="sec-string.prototype.localecompare" para="3" class="theorem">Without ECMA-402 the steps read neither optional parameter: a property of the overlay's steps.</emu-host-law>
  <emu-host-law clause="sec-string.prototype.tolocalelowercase" class="scope">ECMA-402: outside the base layer; without it, the locale-sensitive result is the host choice LocaleLowercase.</emu-host-law>
  <emu-host-law clause="sec-string.prototype.tolocalelowercase" para="3" class="theorem">Without ECMA-402 the steps read neither optional parameter: a property of the overlay's steps.</emu-host-law>
  <emu-host-law clause="sec-string.prototype.tolocaleuppercase" class="scope">ECMA-402: outside the base layer; without it, the locale-sensitive result is the host choice LocaleUppercase.</emu-host-law>
  <emu-host-law clause="sec-string.prototype.tolocaleuppercase" para="3" class="theorem">Without ECMA-402 the steps read neither optional parameter: a property of the overlay's steps.</emu-host-law>
  <emu-host-law clause="sec-array.prototype.tolocalestring" class="scope">ECMA-402 and what an implementation without it may do: outside the base layer.</emu-host-law>
  <emu-host-law clause="sec-%typedarray%.prototype.tolocalestring" class="scope">ECMA-402 and what an implementation without it may do: outside the base layer.</emu-host-law>
  <emu-host-law clause="sec-availablenamedtimezoneidentifiers" class="scope">ECMA-402 and what an implementation without it may do: outside the base layer.</emu-host-law>
  <emu-host-law clause="sec-preparefortailcall" para="0" class="law" law="contextResources">At a push onto the execution context stack, the host's resources run out only past a bound of its own on the contexts whose resources were not discarded (DiscardContextResources), so a chain of tail calls, which does not raise their count, never exhausts them by its length.</emu-host-law>
  <emu-host-law clause="sec-agent-clusters" class="scope">Agent clusters and their embedding: outside the single-agent base layer.</emu-host-law>
  <emu-host-law clause="sec-forbidden-extensions" class="scope">Forbidden extensions: about an implementation's extensions, outside the base layer.</emu-host-law>
  <emu-host-law clause="sec-grouping-operator-static-semantics-early-errors" class="syntax">The cover grammar's refinement: the grammar and its early errors carry it.</emu-host-law>
  <emu-host-law clause="sec-assignment-operators-static-semantics-early-errors" class="syntax">The cover grammar's refinement: the grammar and its early errors carry it.</emu-host-law>
  <emu-host-law clause="sec-destructuring-assignment-static-semantics-early-errors" class="syntax">The cover grammar's refinement: the grammar and its early errors carry it.</emu-host-law>
  <emu-host-law clause="sec-let-and-const-declarations-static-semantics-early-errors" class="syntax">The cover grammar's refinement: the grammar and its early errors carry it.</emu-host-law>
  <emu-host-law clause="sec-for-in-and-for-of-statements-static-semantics-early-errors" class="syntax">The cover grammar's refinement: the grammar and its early errors carry it.</emu-host-law>
  <emu-host-law clause="sec-arrow-function-definitions-static-semantics-early-errors" class="syntax">The cover grammar's refinement: the grammar and its early errors carry it.</emu-host-law>
  <emu-host-law clause="sec-async-arrow-function-definitions-static-semantics-early-errors" class="syntax">The cover grammar's refinement: the grammar and its early errors carry it.</emu-host-law>
  <emu-host-law clause="sec-literals-numeric-literals" class="syntax">A lexical restriction the grammar carries.</emu-host-law>
  <emu-host-law clause="sec-patterns" para="2" class="syntax">The grammar carries it: under the overlay's reading of RegExpUnicodeEscapeSequence (reading-EscapedSurrogatePair), a lone lead is not followed by an escaped trail.</emu-host-law>
  <emu-host-law clause="sec-map-objects" class="nonfunctional">Access time: a cost, not a result.</emu-host-law>
  <emu-host-law clause="sec-set-objects" class="nonfunctional">Access time: a cost, not a result.</emu-host-law>
  <emu-host-law clause="sec-weakmap-objects" class="nonfunctional">Access time: a cost, not a result.</emu-host-law>
